  "sourceState": "Revision 1 is implemented and engine-substrate package green: the typed runtime, durable ports, dispatcher with iteration caps, fail-closed admission over a Harborline-owned capability-authority registry, SoD-gated effect broker, and the two-faced definition-store port (in-process implementation replacing the Shipyard EntityStore topology) with all 157 blocks-workflow ledger cases green natively. The 66 local-node-host durable-seam rows remain open under ticket 074 item 4. Revision 6 (T-488/platform-model-parity) adds the typed envelope with its required Contract, sealed sys.roles, Access-owned role references and narrowing-only standings through model, mapper and admission, proven against the shared hlp.contracts.workflow fixtures. Revision 11 (T-488/interpreter-failure-outcome, ADR-0141/control 1237) records interpreter definition decision errors through the existing atomic advance as Failed/not-retryable naming the actual step, with no effect or retry. Refusals, cancellation and unrelated failures propagate unchanged. Revision 12 (T-1176/platform-gate-instant) carries the act decision instant from one host kernel TimeProvider read to every gate of the act, binds answers to DecidedAt, and ignores trigger time. Revision 13 (T-1176/platform-standing-gate, owner ruling 2026-11-11): WorkflowInstanceCreator loads the admitted pinned definition and refuses a missing or mismatched record-subject reference before persistence. A subjectless or set definition takes no single-record reference. Hosts supply immutable WorkflowSubjectRecordReference (RecordType, RecordId) at creation; the journal persists it and reads it back unchanged. WorkflowGateIntent carries RequiredStandings (every one must hold, decided only by the host) and the stored SubjectRecord; Binds compares every standing and both identity parts. StateJson, trigger payload and dispatch authority never supply the subject. Event-trigger-start supplies the committed event record at creation in its own slice; frozen set membership remains outside this slice. Revision 14 (T-488/operator-migration) adds authorized atomic workflow re-pinning with an explicit step map, preserved state and fenced stale triggers; substrate wait migration belongs to T-528/workflow-run-adoption. Revision 15 (T-488/lifecycle-events) adds a per-run history read on the store port and a versioned, transport-free CNCF Serverless Workflow DSL v1.0.0 fact mapper and execution-runtime wire-name mapping; delivery remains open. Revision 17 (T-488/lifecycle-facts) co-commits pinned WorkflowStarted with creation and mapper-readable task lifecycle history with each advance, including terminal workflowStatus, in version-2 frames; version-1 journals replay unchanged with missing starts left missing.",
